description: graphify knowledge graph — WorkBench + nested project/*/source
alwaysApply: true
---

Two corpora. Pick the graph that matches the code you are exploring — never mix them.

## A. Flow Auto WorkBench (this repo)

- Root / cwd: workspace `.`
- Graph: `graphify-out/graph.json`
- After WorkBench code edits: `graphify update .`

## B. Nested Work / BA checkouts under `project/`

Checkout: `project/<username>/<slug>/source/` (e.g. `project/khoadev/ykk/source`).
BA shared: `project/_ba/<slug>/source/`.

**Graph lives outside source** (WorkBench-owned, never commit into customer git):

- Graph: `project/<username>/<slug>/graphify-out/graph.json`
- Manual rebuild: `scripts/graphify-work-project.sh <username>/<slug>`
- Or: `GRAPHIFY_OUT="$(pwd)/project/<user>/<slug>/graphify-out" graphify update project/<user>/<slug>/source --force`

API auto-runs that update after Work/BA clone (and BA pull) **in the background** — BA Chat / Work continue without waiting for `graphify update` to finish (use the existing map). Disable with `GRAPHIFY_ENABLED=0`.

**BA Chat / workflow:** API runs one short `graphify query`, compacts it to a file list, and injects that "Code map" block. **Work Run/Q&A:** one `code_map_query` (short locator — not the full ticket), then Read the listed files. Do not chain `path` / `explain` unless that list is empty. **Create issue** synthesizes the chat thread only — no graphify, no source read.

Cursor does **not** auto-load nested rules from gitignored `project/`. When the task, open files, Run, or chat target that tree:

1. **Rules first** — `Read` every `…/source/.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and follow them for this session/task (include them in subagent prompts). Do **not** install graphify into customer `source/`.
2. **Graph** — one short query on the sibling graph only:
   - `graphify query "<locator>" --graph project/<user>/<slug>/graphify-out/graph.json`
3. If that `graph.json` is missing, say so and explore with Read/Grep — do **not** fall back to the WorkBench root graph for customer-app questions. You may run `scripts/graphify-work-project.sh <user>/<slug>` to build it.

## One query, then read

Before Grep / Glob / a repo-wide search, run **one** `graphify query "<short locator>"` (with `--graph` for nested). If it lists files, Read 1–3 of them. Do not also run `path` and `explain` unless the query returned no files.

Skip when the target file is already known, or that corpus has no `graphify-out/graph.json` yet. Do not fall back to the WorkBench root graph for customer-app questions.
